Math to LaTeX Android sample

Model: MiniCPM-OCR-1.0 by OpenBMB (https://huggingface.co/openbmb/MiniCPM-OCR-1.0), licensed
under Apache License 2.0. The app downloads its LiteRT-LM conversion,
MiniCPM-OCR-1.0-VL_int8.litertlm, from https://huggingface.co/litert-community/MiniCPM-OCR-1.0
(Apache License 2.0) on first use; the file is not part of this source tree.

app/src/main/java/com/google/ai/edge/examples/math_to_latex/PilBicubic.kt follows the
bicubic resampling of Pillow 13.0.0 (src/libImaging/Resample.c), Copyright (c) 1997-2011
by Secret Labs AB, Copyright (c) 1995-2011 by Fredrik Lundh and contributors, Copyright (c)
2010 by Jeffrey 'Alex' Clark and contributors, under the MIT-CMU License
(licenses/Pillow-MIT-CMU.txt). It is adapted from the Pillow 12.2.0 port of the image cutout sample
proposed in google-ai-edge/litert-samples#490 (samples/litert/image_cutout/kotlin_gpu), with
Pillow 13's choice of which pass runs first.

Pictures.kt follows the picture preparation of the model card's page script, ocr_page.py
(https://github.com/john-rocky/hf-to-litertlm/blob/main/minicpmocr_work/ocr_page.py), whose
slicing grid is that of transformers' MiniCPMOcrImageProcessor.get_sliced_grid (Apache
License 2.0).

The build fetches MathJax 3.2.2 (es5/tex-svg-full.js, https://www.mathjax.org, Apache
License 2.0, licenses/MathJax-APACHE-2.0.txt) into the app's assets to draw the model's
LaTeX; the file is checked against its SHA-256 and is not part of this source tree.

The data package (data/ModelCatalog.kt, data/ModelStore.kt, data/DownloadSafety.kt) is
adapted from this repository's voice assistant sample (samples/litert_lm/voice_assistant).

The example pages app/src/main/assets/examples/*.png were written and rendered for this
sample by tools/make_examples.py: text in DejaVu Serif (Bitstream Vera Fonts license, DejaVu
changes in the public domain), formulas by MathJax.

Gradle wrapper files retain their upstream Apache License 2.0 headers.
Component license texts and their sources are under licenses/.
